  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Which of the following is a type I region in two-dimensional space?",
  "worked_solution": "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14131515/assets/00654c32dbc74614de9b6fdd0f39a5f7d4ecb6ccca0c642ab7ca4a2a8cfe1d89.png)",
